title: Status messages carry Carp's ' at FILE line N.' suffix
updated: 2026-09-27T16:26:59Z
---

Found by k7: errors that come from croak/die end up verbatim in condition messages, e.g. the Ready condition says "...Context not found: dev at lib/Kubernetes/Comb/Upstream/K8s.pm line 172." Status is user-facing (kubectl get combs -o yaml); strip the trailing " at FILE line N." (and a trailing newline) where an exception text becomes a condition message or reason, in one place. Keep the full text available for logs if there is a place for it. Regression test. Do after k9 (POD writer is editing lib/ POD).

2026-09-27 16:24 Cause: Comb.pm _message (the helper every exception->status text goes through) only trims trailing whitespace; the upstream's own status message reaches the Ready condition untouched via _upstream_says. Reproduced: Ready = '...Context not found: dev at lib/Kubernetes/Comb/Upstream/K8s.pm line 172.' and 'check failed: vault sealed at -e line 4.'. Plan: _message strips the Carp/die suffix; _upstream_says runs the upstream's message through _message too (covers every upstream class, not only K8s).

2026-09-27 16:25 Also found (not changed, outside the status path): (1) logs() builds '(no log: ...)' with its own inline trim (Comb.pm ~l.1529), so a log read that croaks still shows ' at FILE line N.' there; could go through _message. (2) Upstream::K8s::_observe (l.179) keeps a private copy of the old _message (whitespace only), so its own status/endpoints answer still carries the suffix for a direct caller; the Comb now cleans it where it becomes status, for any upstream class. (3) deploy()'s failure text 'ensure KIND NAME: <error>' is raw for a direct caller; its status path is cleaned. (4) No log channel exists in the dist, so there is no place to keep the full text beyond what the failing call itself returns.

2026-09-27 16:25 Done: Comb.pm _message, the one helper every error text goes through on its way into status, now also strips the ' at FILE line N.' / ', <FH> line N.' (also '(eval N)') suffix die and croak append; _upstream_says runs the upstream's own status message through it too, which is the path of the reported 'Context not found: dev at .../Upstream/K8s.pm line 172.'. Server text from Kubernetes::REST is untouched apart from that suffix. Tests: t/reconcile.t new subtest (check hook via die, croak, die after reading a handle, string eval, failed Future: Ready and ConfigReady are exactly 'check failed: vault sealed'), t/reconcile-borrow.t Upstream::K8s missing context: Ready ends with 'Context not found: dev'. Red before (10 + 1 failures), green after. prove -lr t/: 22 files, 214 tests, PASS, unit mode (integration skipped, env unset).

